      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ORCHID BOY (5) earns top billing after breaking through at Bathurst, where he worked over the top from a handy position to beat De Razilly by just under a length. The slight concern is coming back from 1200m to 1000m, but he is lightly raced and has Chad Lever back aboard after that win. Since won a trial at Orange over 1000m and has the upside to go on with it. TURF LUCK (2) brings the more reliable overall record, with a Canberra BM50 win two back and a wide run when third in provincial company at Hawkesbury last start. Drops in grade and shapes as the main danger. TENNESSEE DOLLY (4) resumes after five months with two trials behind her and a sound Gosford second before the break, though the 1000m record leaves a small query. SWEET ROSE (3) comes through a Class 2 placing at Queanbeyan, drops back in grade and has not missed a place in three starts, making her a genuine winning hope if she repeats that fresh run.",
